<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <%- include("./partials/head.ejs") %>
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="/styles/texty.css" />
</head>
<body>
    <header>
        <%- include("./partials/navbar.ejs") %>
    </header>
    <main>
        <section>
            <h1>I just got here.</h1>
            <p>
                At the home page, there are a list of games you can choose from (Get there by clicking on the navigation bar title
                at the top left corner). Click on the one you want to play and you will be taken to the game screen.
                There you'll see some input fields for a room code and display name, the game board, some game info and 
                a restart and leave button.
            </p>
            <ul>
                <li>The first of the info shows <span class="green">Connected</span> when you're in a room and Not Connected when you aren't</li>
                <li>The second one shows the piece categories of both you and your opponent, as well as your opponent's display name</li>
                <li>The third one shows whose turn it is. It's <span>green</span> when it's your turn and white when it's not</li>
                <li>The fourth one shows whether you're the room leader or not. 🚫 for not the leader or when you aren't connected and 👑 for when you are.</li>
            </ul>
        </section>
        <section>
            <h1>How to Create/Join A Room</h1>
            <p>
                Within a game screen, type in a room code of your choice. It should be a bit special. This is the code your friend will use to join the room.
                Type that along with your display name and press submit, and that should be it. Both fields must be 30 characters or less.
            </p>
        </section>
        <section>
            <h1>
                What to do when in a game?
            </h1>
            <p>
                Click on <span class="purple">How2Play</span> on the navigation bar to get game specific rules.
                The rules of each game are mostly standard, so if my description isn't enough, you can always look the game up.
                Once you create a room, you can make the first move but will have to wait for an opponent to continue.
                You can also play locally if you have a friend beside you or want to play against the computer, but you shouldn't join any room for that.
                The first person to join a room becomes the room leader. The room leader is the only one who can restart
                the game. When a room leader leaves, the leader role is reassigned randomly.
            </p>
        </section>
        <section>
            <h1>Other stuff</h1>
            <p>
                When you leave a room, depending on the game, the game state is saved until the room leader restarts the game.
                You are disconnected if idle for about 30s.
            </p>
        </section>
    </main>
    <script>
            // definition of variables
            const showNavbarActions = document.getElementById("navbarDropdownButton");
            const navbarLine = document.getElementById("navbarLine");
            const navbarActions = document.getElementById("navbarActions");
            const mediaQuery = window.matchMedia("(max-width: 760px)");
            
            let isNavbarToggled = false;

            // toggle navbar dropdown on or off
            showNavbarActions.addEventListener("click", () => {
                isNavbarToggled = !isNavbarToggled;
                if (isNavbarToggled) {
                    navbarLine.className = "navbar-line";
                    navbarActions.className = "navbar-actions"
                    showNavbarActions.innerHTML = "&#x25B2;";
                } else {
                    navbarLine.className = "navbar-line hidden";
                    navbarActions.className = "navbar-actions hidden";
                    showNavbarActions.innerHTML = "&#x25BC;";
                }
            });
            function handleMediaChange(e) {
                navbarLine.className = "navbar-line hidden";
                isNavbarToggled = false;
                if (e.matches) {
                    showNavbarActions.innerHTML = "&#x25BC;";
                    navbarActions.className = "navbar-actions hidden"
                    showNavbarActions.className = "";
                } else {
                    showNavbarActions.className = "hidden";
                    navbarActions.className = "navbar-actions"
                }
            }
            mediaQuery.addEventListener("change", e => handleMediaChange(e))
            handleMediaChange(mediaQuery);
    </script>
</body>

</html>

